m "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072149/assets/954a3a59a167bd14457d57541e2747f612c5c84ae45cf6b3dc23a534cf354845.png)\n\nConsider the partition of the rectangular region $R$ shown above and the positive function $f(x,y)$ defined on $R.$ Which of the following gives an expression for the lower Riemann sum of $f$ with respect to this partition.\n\n*Hint: ${m}_{ij}$ denotes the minimum value of $f$ on the subregion ${R}_{ij}$*" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the lower Riemann sum $L$ with respect to the given partition, we compute the sum of the volumes of $3$ rectangular solids, one for each ${R}_{ij}.$\n\nThe volume of the rectangular solid corresponding to each subregion ${R}_{ij}$ is given by\n\n$$\n{m}_{ij}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{ij}).\n$$\n\nwhere ${m}_{ij}$ denotes the minimum value of $f$ on the subregion ${R}_{ij}.$ We pick the *minimum* value of $f$ because we're finding the *lower* sum.\n\nSo in our case, we have\n\n$$\nL={m}_{11}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{11})+{m}_{12}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{12})+{m}_{13}\\cdot \\text{Area}({R}_{13}).\n$$\n\nNotice that\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}({R}_{11})=\\text{Area}({R}_{12})=\\text{Area}({R}_{13})=2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L & =2\\cdot {m}_{11}+2\\cdot {m}_{12}+2\\cdot {m}_{13} \\\\  & =2({m}_{11}+{m}_{12}+{m}_{13}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-122877/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c6123a27-2dc8-5076-8c77-1bf056f46566"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-122877"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-122878/selection/48119f95992240b881b55325e9df59d7cc260b669de5151fb05f57d1366d1dac" :answer/id #uuid "fcce5f3a-605d-5233-8276-ee4bf915d1ce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2({m}_{11}+{m}_{21}+{m}_{12}+{m}_{22})" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122878/selection/d8944b76fd87ed9a15cd